1
00:00:05,967 --> 00:00:06,980
[This drama is a work of fiction]

2
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:08,000
[All scenes involving animals and children
were filmed in compliance with regulations]

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,600
[Chungheonmun Gate]

4
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:21,167
Once upon a time,

5
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,567
well, about 13 years ago...

6
00:00:27,567 --> 00:00:29,733
Look over here. One, two...

7
00:00:29,733 --> 00:00:33,400
In the peaceful town of Cheongnam,
where everyone seemed equally happy,

8
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:37,167
there lived a close-knit family.

9
00:00:46,367 --> 00:00:49,467
Come on, pick one before bed. Just pick one.

10
00:00:49,467 --> 00:00:51,300
Min Seo, what's this?

11
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:54,200
- Huh?
- Oh, no, no...

12
00:00:54,933 --> 00:00:56,000
What's this?

13
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,233
The warm-hearted
and generous mother, Soo Jung,

14
00:01:19,967 --> 00:01:23,967
the righteous
and affectionate father, Bo Sung,

15
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:31,700
and their adorable daughter,
Min Seo, who filled their home with laughter.

16
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:35,367
Trusting and relying on one another,

17
00:01:35,367 --> 00:01:39,133
the family lived happily together.

18
00:01:39,133 --> 00:01:44,033
Then I'll take a look
after my appointments tomorrow.

19
00:01:44,033 --> 00:01:48,600
What could our VIP client
possibly mean by that?

20
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:51,100
Dinner?

21
00:01:52,133 --> 00:01:54,300
Perfect. Well, then...

22
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:56,100
Tomorrow...

23
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:59,433
There's a wine bar I like near the hospital.

24
00:01:59,433 --> 00:02:01,967
I'm kind of craving cream pasta.

25
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:10,267
Min Seo, who's this lady?

26
00:02:10,267 --> 00:02:12,167
A friend of Dad's.

27
00:02:42,733 --> 00:02:47,567
[Cheongnam Couple Dermatology Clinic]

28
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:26,433
[81 Missed Calls, Ahn Soo Jung]
Why not make it a hundred, huh?

29
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:28,100
Oh, please...

30
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:30,533
I already cut ties with Eun Kyung, didn't I?

31
00:04:30,533 --> 00:04:34,967
You said divorce was never an option.
Then just pretend you don't know!

32
00:04:36,533 --> 00:04:39,433
What do you expect me to do, then? Huh?

33
00:04:39,433 --> 00:04:41,067
Are you even listening?

34
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:44,867
I've had enough of this, really.

35
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:50,100
Let me breathe a little, okay? Sign it.

36
00:04:58,633 --> 00:05:01,700
[Petition for Confirmation of Mutual Divorce]

37
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:06,433
Get in.

38
00:05:06,433 --> 00:05:09,400
Let's go, let's go!

39
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:10,800
No, no, not Schweitzer!

40
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,333
- Not Schweitzer...
- Move!

41
00:05:12,333 --> 00:05:14,700
He's my baby. I adopted him. Let's go!

42
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:18,333
- Not Schweitzer! Please, not Schweitzer...
- It's okay, it's okay.

43
00:05:37,033 --> 00:05:41,300
[Cheongnam Crystal Dermatology,
Dermatologist, Chief Director Ahn Soo Jung]

44
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:53,767
[Cheongnam Crystal Dermatology]

45
00:05:53,767 --> 00:05:56,933
[Middle School Medical School Prep Roadmap]

46
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:13,300
[Arts High School Admissions:
Department & Audition Strategy Seminar]

47
00:06:16,667 --> 00:06:19,500
I told you not to rummage through my room!

48
00:06:25,767 --> 00:06:30,033
Did you get counseling
for arts high school behind my back?

49
00:06:31,233 --> 00:06:34,833
You can draw as a hobby all you want.

50
00:06:34,833 --> 00:06:37,300
I told you, it's not a hobby!

51
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:39,200
How many times do I have to tell you? I...

52
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:42,433
I'm only worried about you, Min Seo.

53
00:06:42,433 --> 00:06:44,800
It was hard enough getting you
into the med school prep class.

54
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:47,000
What if you fall behind and get pushed out...

55
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,600
I'm already at the bottom of the class!

56
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:51,600
I'm not good at studying!

57
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,733
No, you're not.

58
00:06:52,733 --> 00:06:55,367
How could you not be good at studying?
You're my daughter.

59
00:06:55,367 --> 00:06:58,433
Didn't I tell you?
I was always at the top of my class.

60
00:06:58,433 --> 00:07:01,800
This is what I want to do!

61
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,900
Dad understands everything.

62
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:07,200
He says I can do whatever I want!
Why can't you?

63
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:10,300
I can't breathe because of you!

64
00:07:13,467 --> 00:07:15,633
I want to live with Dad.

65
00:07:15,633 --> 00:07:17,967
Seriously...

66
00:07:25,367 --> 00:07:28,967
Do you really think your dad
would welcome you with open arms?

67
00:07:28,967 --> 00:07:30,600
Don't you remember?

68
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:35,200
Don't you remember when he left this house,
he only took Schweitzer?

69
00:07:37,900 --> 00:07:39,767
Yesterday, no...

70
00:07:39,767 --> 00:07:42,900
I went too far yesterday, no...

71
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:46,100
I'm sorry about yesterday. But you also...

72
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,833
I...

73
00:07:49,833 --> 00:07:53,967
Min... Min Seo. Min Seo? Min Seo!

74
00:07:59,367 --> 00:08:01,067
Min Seo!

75
00:08:01,067 --> 00:08:04,600
Are you sure you don't want a ride?

76
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:07,133
- Hello!
- Hello.

77
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,667
[Episode 2, The Woman Next Door]

78
00:08:48,667 --> 00:08:50,767
Oh, this is nice.

79
00:08:50,767 --> 00:08:54,200
This can really improve elasticity that much?

80
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:57,867
It's great for volume and firmness.

81
00:08:57,867 --> 00:09:01,833
You'll notice the results right away.

82
00:09:01,833 --> 00:09:06,333
There's another kind of volume
I'd rather improve...

83
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:12,767
- The setting's okay, right?
- Yeah.

84
00:09:12,767 --> 00:09:16,000
By the way, are you keeping your clinic open?

85
00:09:17,067 --> 00:09:18,800
Pardon?

86
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:21,500
Yesterday, Dr. Joo sent out a text...

87
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:27,433
Oh dear... did I say
something I shouldn't have?

88
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:34,433
- Here I go.
- Okay.

89
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:37,700
I'm a true crew member

90
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:38,867
since when there were only ten subscribers.

91
00:09:38,867 --> 00:09:41,700
- Oh, I see.
- I've bought every single piece of merch.

92
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:44,767
- That's amazing, since ten subscribers?
- Yeah.

93
00:09:44,767 --> 00:09:46,667
If you bring her,

94
00:09:46,667 --> 00:09:49,500
I'll secretly give you service
without the director knowing.

95
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:51,100
- That's awesome.
- Bring her over.

96
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:53,633
- I will.
- Hello.

97
00:09:53,633 --> 00:09:55,800
Oh, hello.

98
00:09:56,667 --> 00:10:01,500
Wow, you look completely different
in a doctor's gown.

99
00:10:03,433 --> 00:10:04,767
This is Ms. Ryu Ji Su.

100
00:10:04,767 --> 00:10:06,767
Hello!

101
00:10:06,767 --> 00:10:07,833
Hi.

102
00:10:07,833 --> 00:10:11,167
Ji Su, this is the director
I told you about who lives next door.

103
00:10:11,167 --> 00:10:13,433
She's absolutely gorgeous.

104
00:10:14,733 --> 00:10:17,400
I've been working hard to promote you.

105
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:19,100
Okay.

106
00:10:21,533 --> 00:10:23,267
[Honey]

107
00:10:25,667 --> 00:10:27,367
Yeah, honey.

108
00:10:27,367 --> 00:10:28,967
Yeah.

109
00:10:30,167 --> 00:10:31,933
Huh?

110
00:10:31,933 --> 00:10:33,700
Oh...

111
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:35,200
Of course, yeah.

112
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,567
Yeah, hold on, hold on.

113
00:10:36,567 --> 00:10:38,667
- Thank you for your hard work!
- Thank you.

114
00:10:38,667 --> 00:10:39,867
Yeah.

115
00:10:39,867 --> 00:10:42,933
Boo Jin, could you take care of
Ms. Ryu's post-treatment care?

116
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:44,067
Sure.

117
00:10:44,067 --> 00:10:45,733
Well, Director.

118
00:10:45,733 --> 00:10:47,567
Huh?

119
00:10:47,567 --> 00:10:50,367
I have something to show you.

120
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:56,133
Dr. Joo sent this text to patients,
making it sound like

121
00:10:56,133 --> 00:10:58,000
our clinic is shutting down.

122
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:02,200
He also said he's opening a new clinic
in the neighboring complex.

123
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:15,567
[How to Use the Fire Hose Cabinet]

124
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:23,233
What are you up to? Huh?

125
00:11:23,233 --> 00:11:26,600
Why are you spreading lies to our patients?

126
00:11:27,533 --> 00:11:29,900
How about Kang Tae Han?
He's a box-office star. She'd be thrilled.

127
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:32,900
How am I supposed to bring him along?

128
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,800
He probably has a dermatologist he goes to.

129
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:36,400
- Then this is the perfect chance to switch.
- Huh?

130
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:40,733
Anyway, Hong, use any means necessary,
just bring him in no matter what.

131
00:11:40,733 --> 00:11:43,467
Okay, fine. I'll talk to him first.

132
00:11:43,467 --> 00:11:44,800
Yeah, make sure you do.

133
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:46,767
Okay.

134
00:11:46,767 --> 00:11:49,200
You were the one who changed the passcode

135
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:51,333
to the second house without telling me.

136
00:11:51,333 --> 00:11:53,700
Back then, do you have any idea
how much trouble that caused me?

137
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:56,933
Why? Did you take another woman there?

138
00:11:56,933 --> 00:11:59,900
I'm filing for custody. Just so you know.

139
00:12:00,767 --> 00:12:03,300
- Excuse...
- You're the one who abandoned Min Seo!

140
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:06,500
How dare you talk about custody now?

141
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:10,133
Min Seo wants to live with me too.
Whatever. I'm hanging up.

142
00:12:21,567 --> 00:12:24,133
What? What's wrong with this?

143
00:12:26,833 --> 00:12:28,733
What?

144
00:12:28,733 --> 00:12:32,100
What's wrong with this?

145
00:12:34,033 --> 00:12:35,067
Hello.

146
00:12:35,067 --> 00:12:38,500
What are you doing?
Were you eavesdropping on my call?

147
00:12:39,533 --> 00:12:41,033
Eavesdropping?

148
00:12:41,033 --> 00:12:43,767
I was here first, on my phone.

149
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:47,367
Then you could've at least
let me know you are here.

150
00:12:47,367 --> 00:12:50,567
I actually tried to say hello earlier, but...

151
00:12:50,567 --> 00:12:52,367
The fire...

152
00:12:53,333 --> 00:12:55,300
There's a fire!

153
00:12:56,833 --> 00:12:59,600
Wait, wait, it's dangerous!
Don't get close. Hold on, hold on.

154
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:01,533
Wait, what is this?

155
00:13:01,533 --> 00:13:04,233
W-What did you put in it?

156
00:13:20,033 --> 00:13:21,667
Here, here!

157
00:13:22,867 --> 00:13:26,100
When you put out this kind of fire,
you have to cut off the oxygen first.

158
00:13:35,567 --> 00:13:37,167
What is this?

159
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:52,267
That could've been bad.

160
00:13:53,233 --> 00:13:54,867
Thank you.

161
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:01,433
Where exactly were you
trying to aim the extinguisher?

162
00:14:15,767 --> 00:14:17,733
It's okay now.

163
00:14:20,367 --> 00:14:23,900
I know this isn't really my place, but...

164
00:14:24,733 --> 00:14:28,733
Min Seo's father is a parent too.

165
00:14:28,733 --> 00:14:32,000
How can he use his own child
as a bargaining chip?

166
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,200
Seriously.

167
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:37,267
In a case like this, you should just
take it all the way to court, you know?

168
00:14:37,267 --> 00:14:40,467
You have to fight tooth and nail
and take him for everything he's got.

169
00:14:40,467 --> 00:14:44,667
Thank you, I'll take him
for everything he's got.

170
00:14:45,833 --> 00:14:47,400
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

171
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:48,567
Hello, yeah.

172
00:14:48,567 --> 00:14:50,067
This is my senior actor, Kang Tae Han.

173
00:14:50,067 --> 00:14:51,667
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you. I'm Kang Tae Han.

174
00:14:51,667 --> 00:14:55,333
Yes, I've really enjoyed your work.
Nice to meet you.

175
00:14:57,133 --> 00:15:00,267
After you're done with your appointment,
could we maybe take a photo...

176
00:15:00,267 --> 00:15:01,767
- A picture? Sure, anytime.
- Is that okay?

177
00:15:01,767 --> 00:15:03,933
- Of course. I'd be happy to.
- Thank you.

178
00:15:03,933 --> 00:15:05,567
I'll take a selfie for you.

179
00:15:05,567 --> 00:15:06,633
One, two...

180
00:15:06,633 --> 00:15:08,467
- Hello.
- Hello.

181
00:15:08,467 --> 00:15:09,867
Oh, this is mine.

182
00:15:09,867 --> 00:15:11,367
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

183
00:15:11,367 --> 00:15:14,467
This is mine, so I'll send it
to you after we're done.

184
00:15:14,467 --> 00:15:16,433
- This is my senior actor, Kang Tae Han.
- Oh, yes.

185
00:15:16,433 --> 00:15:17,533
- Hello, I'm Kang Tae Han.
- This is the director.

186
00:15:17,533 --> 00:15:19,333
- Oh, Director.
- Hello.

187
00:15:20,567 --> 00:15:22,767
Then we can take the picture later,
after we're done, right?

188
00:15:22,767 --> 00:15:24,400
Yes.

189
00:15:42,267 --> 00:15:44,233
[@Chastaryobb_ Love today's outfit]

190
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:51,800
Wow, this is really neat.

191
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:57,233
Anyway, you two look so happy together.

192
00:16:57,233 --> 00:17:00,000
But aren't you a little worried?

193
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:03,333
I saw at the hospital
that your husband is still very popular.

194
00:17:03,333 --> 00:17:07,033
- Oh, not at all.
- It's good if an actor is popular.

195
00:17:07,033 --> 00:17:11,900
Even Ms. Ryu Ji Su calls him oppa
and is naturally touchy-feely.

196
00:17:12,700 --> 00:17:15,300
Oh my, be careful.

197
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:17,533
Oh, what do I do? I'm sorry.
Did it splash on this thing?

198
00:17:17,533 --> 00:17:18,933
The furniture is fine.

199
00:17:18,933 --> 00:17:21,633
Your clothes got stained though.
Go clean it up quickly.

200
00:17:21,633 --> 00:17:24,300
- It's all over your clothes.
- It's fine. Are you okay?

201
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:25,867
- Yeah, I'm fine.
- Oh, jeez...

202
00:17:25,867 --> 00:17:27,400
- Where can I find...
- Down the hall

203
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:29,100
- Oh, yes.
- at the end.

204
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:31,600
Oh, what a mess.

205
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:33,767
- Are you okay?
- What? Oh, I...

206
00:17:33,767 --> 00:17:35,967
Be careful.

207
00:17:35,967 --> 00:17:37,200
- I'll...
- Please be careful.

208
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,833
Yeah.

209
00:17:40,133 --> 00:17:44,167
Something always happens
whenever we meet, doesn't it?

210
00:17:45,533 --> 00:17:47,200
I know, right?

211
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:53,233
At this rate, are we going to
have a car accident next time?

212
00:17:59,667 --> 00:18:02,167
- Oh my, you're bleeding here.
- What?

213
00:18:03,433 --> 00:18:05,867
- I'm fine.
- Would you like to go to the guest room?

214
00:18:05,867 --> 00:18:07,300
There's a first-aid kit there.

215
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:11,267
It's not a deep cut,
but it could still get infected.

216
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:14,167
Oh, really?

217
00:18:17,567 --> 00:18:19,600
It might sting a little.

218
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:51,767
I-I still need to finish the dressing...

219
00:18:51,767 --> 00:18:55,000
Yeah, you should dress it.

220
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:12,500
- Are you okay?
- What?

221
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:13,533
Huh?

222
00:19:13,533 --> 00:19:15,533
- Why are you coming out from there?
- Oh.

223
00:19:15,533 --> 00:19:17,333
I cut my hand earlier.

224
00:19:17,333 --> 00:19:19,167
Jeez, let me see.

225
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:23,500
It's fine.

226
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,633
- Look at this bandage job.
- The bandage is all crumpled.

227
00:19:25,633 --> 00:19:27,167
That's a pretty deep cut. Huh?

228
00:19:27,167 --> 00:19:28,833
It's done now.

229
00:19:30,133 --> 00:19:31,667
Oh, right.

230
00:19:31,667 --> 00:19:37,133
I'll arrange a meeting with Aunt Michelle.

231
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:43,867
We should help each other out.
We're neighbors, after all.

232
00:19:46,133 --> 00:19:49,767
[Autonomous driving mode]

233
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:55,500
[Please take control of the steering wheel]

234
00:20:05,167 --> 00:20:07,600
We almost ended up dead.

235
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:09,533
That startled me.

236
00:20:10,967 --> 00:20:13,067
Oh, honey.

237
00:20:13,067 --> 00:20:15,000
That was dangerous.

238
00:20:35,367 --> 00:20:36,433
[Are things going well with Aunt Michelle?]

239
00:20:36,433 --> 00:20:37,633
[No, she's still not here]

240
00:20:37,633 --> 00:20:38,633
[Really? She's not the type to be late]

241
00:20:38,633 --> 00:20:40,267
[I miss you]

242
00:20:48,767 --> 00:20:50,567
Min Seo!

243
00:20:50,567 --> 00:20:52,333
What are you doing there?

244
00:20:58,167 --> 00:21:01,267
Why? Are you going to tear it up again?

245
00:21:04,667 --> 00:21:06,637
[It would be nice if we could eat together.]

246
00:21:06,637 --> 00:21:07,870
[Actually, what I really want is...]

247
00:21:07,870 --> 00:21:09,100
[You know it's you, right?]

248
00:21:13,867 --> 00:21:16,500
It's still chilly out here.

249
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:18,367
Go inside and draw.

250
00:21:33,267 --> 00:21:34,267
[Courtroom 416, Court in Session]

251
00:21:34,267 --> 00:21:37,000
Today is just a formality
to confirm a few things.

252
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:40,167
Oh, hello. It's been a while.

253
00:21:40,167 --> 00:21:44,733
Hello, I'm Choi Sang Cheol,
the attorney representing your husband.

254
00:21:44,733 --> 00:21:46,933
Oh, I see.

255
00:21:49,767 --> 00:21:51,900
This is going to be a headache.

256
00:21:51,900 --> 00:21:53,267
Why?

257
00:21:53,267 --> 00:21:56,067
Just, for someone who calls himself a lawyer,

258
00:21:56,067 --> 00:21:59,367
he's always pulling stunts
outside the courtroom.

259
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:01,333
You are here.

260
00:22:01,333 --> 00:22:02,600
You came early.

261
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:04,600
Traffic was bad.

262
00:22:05,233 --> 00:22:08,667
As I mentioned,
this shouldn't take too long today.

263
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:14,033
- I'm worried.
- About what?

264
00:22:14,033 --> 00:22:17,867
I asked around,
and turns out, this Choi Sang Cheol thinks

265
00:22:17,867 --> 00:22:20,367
illegal recording and stalking
are just part of the job.

266
00:22:20,367 --> 00:22:23,767
He's not a lawyer.
He's nothing but a lowlife thug.

267
00:22:23,767 --> 00:22:25,233
Yeah?

268
00:22:25,233 --> 00:22:27,533
Then you need to fight back just as hard.

269
00:22:27,533 --> 00:22:29,633
People like that...

270
00:22:31,900 --> 00:22:35,100
Oh, honey, should I introduce you
to a private investigator?

271
00:22:35,867 --> 00:22:37,433
I don't think I need to go that far.

272
00:22:37,433 --> 00:22:40,800
I mean, you said he cheated on you

273
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:42,967
more than once
when you two were living together.

274
00:22:42,967 --> 00:22:47,733
So if we dig into his background a little,
don't you think we'll find something?

275
00:22:47,733 --> 00:22:49,967
- You know Park & Jeong, right?
- Yeah.

276
00:22:49,967 --> 00:22:53,500
They're one of the top divorce law firms.

277
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:55,300
You know, when our CEO got divorced,

278
00:22:55,300 --> 00:22:59,467
she trusted their reputation
and handed everything over to them.

279
00:22:59,467 --> 00:23:03,967
And she almost lost everything,
the Cheongnam apartment, her son, everything.

280
00:23:03,967 --> 00:23:06,067
In the end, out of desperation,

281
00:23:06,067 --> 00:23:09,233
she hired a private investigator
as a last resort...

282
00:23:09,233 --> 00:23:11,133
- Oh, it's hot!
- Sorry, sorry.

283
00:23:11,133 --> 00:23:12,733
Is it hot?

284
00:23:15,433 --> 00:23:17,467
- Are you alright?
- Yeah.

285
00:23:18,233 --> 00:23:20,933
Anyway, she hired
a private investigator back then

286
00:23:20,933 --> 00:23:23,800
and had them quietly look into her husband.

287
00:23:23,800 --> 00:23:26,833
And just like that,
everything was taken care of in one go.

288
00:23:28,133 --> 00:23:31,767
What do you think?
Should I get you the number?

289
00:23:32,967 --> 00:23:35,433
It's okay. Don't worry about it.

290
00:23:35,433 --> 00:23:38,300
You're probably stressed enough
because of those rumors.

291
00:23:38,300 --> 00:23:40,433
Yeah, tell me about it.

292
00:23:41,167 --> 00:23:44,400
I mean, how did I end up in a scandal
with Ryu Ji Su? It's ridiculous.

293
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:46,067
You're right.

294
00:23:48,033 --> 00:23:49,433
All done?

295
00:23:49,433 --> 00:23:51,200
You look pretty.

296
00:24:22,067 --> 00:24:25,000
I like this part.

297
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:27,900
Who is this? Liv? Jenny?

298
00:24:27,900 --> 00:24:30,433
It's not Jenny, it's Jenna.

299
00:24:30,433 --> 00:24:32,067
Oh...

300
00:24:33,733 --> 00:24:35,667
You've got a message.

301
00:24:40,500 --> 00:24:43,533
Mom, do you need money?

302
00:24:43,533 --> 00:24:46,133
Huh? Why do you ask?

303
00:24:46,133 --> 00:24:48,100
Because you've been using
Gogo Used Market a lot lately.

304
00:24:48,100 --> 00:24:50,967
Oh, no, no.

305
00:24:50,967 --> 00:24:52,633
That's not it.

306
00:24:52,633 --> 00:24:55,900
Your ring is pretty. Did Dad give it to you?

307
00:24:57,033 --> 00:24:58,700
Yeah.

308
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:16,833
Mom, has something good happened lately?

309
00:25:17,567 --> 00:25:19,133
No, why?

310
00:25:19,133 --> 00:25:21,900
You just seem happier these days.

311
00:25:21,900 --> 00:25:25,367
Oh, no, it's just that...

312
00:25:25,367 --> 00:25:28,200
You have seemed happier lately

313
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:32,000
and seeing that makes me happy too, Min Seo.

314
00:25:45,067 --> 00:25:47,267
[Lim Ye Ji: Min Seo, is something
going on at your house?]

315
00:25:47,267 --> 00:25:49,833
[Right now, in front of your house...]

316
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:54,567
Huh? What is it?

317
00:25:55,600 --> 00:25:57,867
Huh? Wait...

318
00:25:57,867 --> 00:25:59,833
Why are there so many police officers here?

319
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:15,367
She said she wants to die.
The girl said she wants to die.

320
00:26:15,367 --> 00:26:17,600
If this isn't abuse, then what is?

321
00:26:21,300 --> 00:26:22,367
Come quickly. Hurry.

322
00:26:22,367 --> 00:26:25,000
She's a child abuser.
Please arrest her quickly.

323
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,167
Please separate them. Quickly.

324
00:26:26,167 --> 00:26:28,300
Now, wait, just a moment.

325
00:26:28,300 --> 00:26:29,667
Are you saying it's child abuse?

326
00:26:29,667 --> 00:26:31,033
How shameless.

327
00:26:31,033 --> 00:26:33,600
Sir, please calm down.

328
00:26:33,600 --> 00:26:36,367
Could we speak with Min Seo first?

329
00:26:36,367 --> 00:26:38,700
We just need to ask her a few questions.

330
00:26:40,700 --> 00:26:42,367
Wait...

331
00:26:56,233 --> 00:26:57,567
Did you go to your dad again?

332
00:26:57,567 --> 00:27:00,300
Why didn't you tell me?

333
00:27:00,300 --> 00:27:02,933
Mom, I...

334
00:27:02,933 --> 00:27:05,433
You should've told me yourself.

335
00:27:05,433 --> 00:27:07,776
That I monitor you, tear up your drawings,

336
00:27:07,776 --> 00:27:10,267
and make you so suffocated you wanna die...

337
00:27:10,267 --> 00:27:14,000
You didn't have to make them all hear this.

338
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:18,800
That's... I didn't even know
Dad was recording.

339
00:27:18,800 --> 00:27:21,967
I never thought he'd use my words like this.

340
00:27:21,967 --> 00:27:24,167
But I told the police it was all in the past

341
00:27:24,167 --> 00:27:26,333
and that things are okay now.

342
00:27:26,333 --> 00:27:30,767
- It'll be okay.
- It's not okay at all, Min Seo! This...

343
00:27:30,767 --> 00:27:32,900
What else did you tell your Dad about me?

344
00:27:32,900 --> 00:27:35,633
What did you hand over to that lawyer
that made him so sure of himself,

345
00:27:35,633 --> 00:27:37,533
claiming he has tons of evidence of abuse?

346
00:27:37,533 --> 00:27:39,400
Huh? Min Seo...

347
00:27:50,233 --> 00:27:52,333
Alright.

348
00:27:52,333 --> 00:27:54,167
Min Seo?

349
00:27:54,167 --> 00:27:59,100
Do you want to talk about how hurt you were
when your Dad left home?

350
00:27:59,100 --> 00:28:01,567
Or how he was indifferent
when you were little?

351
00:28:01,567 --> 00:28:03,767
Or any other mistakes he made?

352
00:28:03,767 --> 00:28:07,233
Just tell me everything comfortably.
You can tell me, can't you?

353
00:28:10,567 --> 00:28:12,667
Why aren't you saying anything? Why?

354
00:28:12,667 --> 00:28:15,300
You badmouthed me like that,
but what's so great about that man...

355
00:28:15,300 --> 00:28:17,300
Oh, please!

356
00:28:17,300 --> 00:28:19,567
You two are getting divorced.

357
00:28:20,667 --> 00:28:23,300
So why are you doing this to me?

358
00:28:24,233 --> 00:28:27,267
I thought you were being nicer lately,
but you're still the same.

359
00:29:05,667 --> 00:29:07,267
[I'm here to pick up Min Seo]

360
00:29:07,267 --> 00:29:08,900
[You must be tired, honey. I miss you]

361
00:29:08,900 --> 00:29:13,067
[Could you look into that PI's office
you mentioned before?]

362
00:29:13,067 --> 00:29:16,133
21 Bonggak-dong.

363
00:29:16,133 --> 00:29:19,367
Huh? What's this?

364
00:29:19,367 --> 00:29:21,100
Why isn't it showing up?

365
00:29:23,133 --> 00:29:25,033
Oh, you're here?

366
00:29:27,100 --> 00:29:28,300
That's strange.

367
00:29:28,300 --> 00:29:31,100
21 Bonggak-dong... Why isn't it
showing up on the navigation?

368
00:29:31,100 --> 00:29:32,833
Is it not there?

369
00:29:34,167 --> 00:29:37,033
[Please enter the full name, initials,
phone number, or address]

370
00:29:37,033 --> 00:29:40,300
21 Bonggak-dong!

371
00:29:40,300 --> 00:29:43,000
This address no longer exists.

372
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:46,333
- What?
- Shall I direct you to the previous address?

373
00:29:49,200 --> 00:29:51,733
Yes, navigate.

374
00:29:53,333 --> 00:29:54,933
- Oh, it's showing up.
- Starting navigation.

375
00:29:54,933 --> 00:29:56,667
It's not far from here.

376
00:29:56,667 --> 00:29:58,200
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

377
00:29:58,200 --> 00:30:00,767
- Put on your seat belt.
- Okay.

378
00:30:03,200 --> 00:30:05,767
[21 Bonggak-dong, Yongun City]

379
00:30:08,133 --> 00:30:12,033
[Strongly oppose reckless redevelopment]

380
00:30:12,033 --> 00:30:16,633
[My home value is plummeting,
residents are crying]

381
00:30:24,467 --> 00:30:27,400
I can't be seen in a place like this.

382
00:30:29,167 --> 00:30:32,267
Yeah, I understand.

383
00:30:38,233 --> 00:30:42,133
[T.D.A]

384
00:30:57,967 --> 00:30:59,933
Oh, what brings you here?

385
00:30:59,933 --> 00:31:01,833
Oh, yes, hello.

386
00:31:01,833 --> 00:31:04,567
I was referred here.

387
00:31:07,400 --> 00:31:10,067
Yes, please have a seat
over here for a moment.

388
00:31:20,233 --> 00:31:25,300
[Manager Na Sol, Twin Detective Agency]

389
00:31:34,700 --> 00:31:36,700
Hello.

390
00:31:36,700 --> 00:31:37,700
Yeah.

391
00:31:37,700 --> 00:31:39,867
You called earlier, right?

392
00:31:39,867 --> 00:31:41,933
Oh, yes.

393
00:31:41,933 --> 00:31:44,700
Well, I heard the gist of it.

394
00:31:44,700 --> 00:31:49,967
You're fighting for custody
against your cheating, worthless husband.

395
00:31:51,267 --> 00:31:54,240
You need evidence, but you don't want it

396
00:31:54,240 --> 00:31:56,800
to look like
you hired a private investigator, right?

397
00:31:56,800 --> 00:31:57,967
But, the thing is

398
00:31:57,967 --> 00:32:02,033
privacy laws are pretty strict,
so digging up information isn't easy.

399
00:32:02,033 --> 00:32:06,267
And even if we don't find anything,
you'll still have to pay the fee.

400
00:32:07,033 --> 00:32:10,433
That's why we usually don't take cases
that require this much work.

401
00:32:10,433 --> 00:32:13,333
Huh? Wait a moment.

402
00:32:14,016 --> 00:32:17,388
Crap.

403
00:32:21,033 --> 00:32:23,333
I'm sorry, maybe another time.

404
00:32:24,833 --> 00:32:26,933
Sure, come again if you need anything.

405
00:32:34,267 --> 00:32:35,933
What?

406
00:32:38,467 --> 00:32:40,200
Hold on, hold on!

407
00:32:40,200 --> 00:32:42,167
You should at least hear me out.

408
00:32:42,167 --> 00:32:44,077
- No, it's okay.
- We usually don't take cases

409
00:32:44,077 --> 00:32:45,300
that require this much effort.

410
00:32:45,300 --> 00:32:47,867
But you said your husband
is a real piece of work.

411
00:32:47,867 --> 00:32:49,867
So we'll make an exception for you.

412
00:32:49,867 --> 00:32:52,367
- No.
- I hear there are a lot of

413
00:32:52,367 --> 00:32:56,300
detective agencies these days
that scam their own clients.

414
00:32:56,300 --> 00:32:58,100
It's fine.

415
00:32:58,100 --> 00:33:02,700
Don't end up regretting it after losing
your child to that lousy husband.

416
00:33:10,633 --> 00:33:16,600
Is there a way to make sure I win?

417
00:33:16,600 --> 00:33:19,233
Well, we'll have to find one.

418
00:33:19,233 --> 00:33:25,800
But usually, these things work out.
It'll just cost a little extra.

419
00:33:25,800 --> 00:33:27,400
Yeah.

420
00:33:33,233 --> 00:33:35,533
- Hello.
- Why are you sitting here? You startled me.

421
00:33:35,533 --> 00:33:37,900
- Have you eaten?
- Yes, I have.

422
00:33:37,900 --> 00:33:38,900
[Gogo Used Market, Wang Jae]

423
00:33:38,900 --> 00:33:40,167
[Congrats on your first ad!]

424
00:33:40,167 --> 00:33:42,233
[Thanks, I feel like things have been
going well ever since I met you]

425
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:57,333
Oh, Director...

426
00:33:58,000 --> 00:34:00,667
about Jae Hong...

427
00:34:00,667 --> 00:34:05,000
I mean, at the clinic, Ryu Ji Su...

428
00:34:06,267 --> 00:34:08,700
Never mind. Have a good day.

429
00:34:08,700 --> 00:34:10,300
Yeah.

430
00:34:25,567 --> 00:34:31,033
[The Day of the Accident]

431
00:34:46,976 --> 00:34:49,467
Let's hurry up and go over there.

432
00:34:49,467 --> 00:34:51,000
- Please come visit us.
- What is this?

433
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:52,567
Please come visit us. We'll do our best.

434
00:34:52,567 --> 00:34:54,033
- What is this? What is this?
- Thank you.

435
00:34:54,033 --> 00:34:56,867
[24-Hour Unlimited Choice, Unlimited Touch,
Ladies Always Available]

436
00:34:56,867 --> 00:34:58,700
- No, I'm not going. Forget it.
- You're not going?

437
00:34:58,700 --> 00:35:01,400
- We can go if you want.
- Let's just have a drink. What nonsense.

438
00:35:16,900 --> 00:35:18,367
Did you finish it or not?

439
00:35:18,367 --> 00:35:20,667
- You drank it? You did?
- I finished it all, all of it.

440
00:35:20,667 --> 00:35:22,900
Ji Young, you come here too.

441
00:35:22,900 --> 00:35:24,367
No, no...

442
00:35:24,367 --> 00:35:25,900
Huh? What's this?

443
00:35:25,900 --> 00:35:27,700
I'm not used to this kind of thing...

444
00:35:53,600 --> 00:35:57,033
We'll make sure you're comfortable, lawyer.

445
00:35:57,033 --> 00:35:58,900
[Your husband's lawyer
has a lot of dirty tricks]

446
00:35:58,900 --> 00:36:02,067
[I'll see if I can get him on our side]

447
00:36:05,600 --> 00:36:09,333
- Huh?
- Director, aren't you heading home?

448
00:36:09,333 --> 00:36:11,933
You can go home.

449
00:36:13,200 --> 00:36:15,633
I'll head out then.

450
00:36:15,633 --> 00:36:17,433
Okay.

451
00:36:34,700 --> 00:36:37,300
Darn it, he's sleeping like a log.

452
00:36:49,533 --> 00:36:51,167
Excuse me.

453
00:36:52,700 --> 00:36:54,367
[Cheongnam Crystal Dermatology]
Excuse me?

454
00:36:56,500 --> 00:36:58,767
What? What if someone sees us?

455
00:36:58,767 --> 00:37:00,667
I sent all the staff home.

456
00:37:00,667 --> 00:37:02,300
Yeah?

457
00:37:04,600 --> 00:37:06,233
Good job.

458
00:37:09,300 --> 00:37:10,667
Mister!

459
00:37:10,667 --> 00:37:13,333
Wake up, okay?

460
00:37:14,167 --> 00:37:19,633
Since you're a lawyer,
I guess I don't need to explain much.

461
00:37:19,633 --> 00:37:21,100
About the minor.

462
00:37:21,100 --> 00:37:24,700
Illegal filming
and even sexual assault. Oh, dear.

463
00:37:24,700 --> 00:37:26,233
She's not a minor, she's not...

464
00:37:26,233 --> 00:37:30,400
- It wasn't sexual assault. No, no, no.
- But, this belongs to you, doesn't it?

465
00:37:30,400 --> 00:37:34,733
The more I looked into this,
the more suspicious things I found.

466
00:37:34,733 --> 00:37:37,767
If I knew it was going to be like this,
I would've just caught you.

467
00:37:37,767 --> 00:37:42,233
Wait, wait, wait...

468
00:37:42,233 --> 00:37:47,104
- Where are you going?
- Hold on, hold on.

469
00:37:50,167 --> 00:37:53,233
Sir, how about this? I'll give you money.

470
00:37:53,233 --> 00:37:54,633
Whatever you want, I'll...

471
00:37:54,633 --> 00:37:56,633
Well, it's worth hundreds
of millions of won, but...

472
00:37:56,633 --> 00:37:58,433
I also have a duty to my client.

473
00:37:58,433 --> 00:38:01,467
- Client? Who's your client?
- That's none of your business.

474
00:38:01,467 --> 00:38:03,667
Well, you know Joo Bo Sung, right?

475
00:38:03,667 --> 00:38:06,500
I heard you've taken on his custody case.

476
00:38:06,500 --> 00:38:09,567
Lose that case cleanly,
and I'll give this back to you.

477
00:38:09,567 --> 00:38:13,700
So, what do you say? Huh?

478
00:38:13,700 --> 00:38:18,900
Anyway, lawyers never give a darn answer.

479
00:38:21,267 --> 00:38:23,933
Sang Cheol! Look here.

480
00:38:23,933 --> 00:38:27,367
There's no CCTV here,
and no one comes around.

481
00:38:27,367 --> 00:38:30,633
I could do whatever I want to you,

482
00:38:30,633 --> 00:38:33,600
and no one would come!

483
00:38:38,767 --> 00:38:42,033
I was actually about to call you.

484
00:38:42,033 --> 00:38:44,333
- We're totally in sync.
- Yeah?

485
00:38:44,333 --> 00:38:46,933
You know the place
you introduced me to last time?

486
00:38:46,933 --> 00:38:50,133
It's a little unusual,
but they seem good at what they do.

487
00:38:50,133 --> 00:38:51,600
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

488
00:38:51,600 --> 00:38:52,900
That's a relief.

489
00:38:52,900 --> 00:38:55,800
I was really struggling because of that.

490
00:38:55,800 --> 00:38:58,167
In return, charge me up now.

491
00:38:58,867 --> 00:39:02,133
Now? Really? Here?

492
00:39:07,533 --> 00:39:08,633
Ta-da!

493
00:39:08,633 --> 00:39:11,767
What? You prepared this too?

494
00:39:11,767 --> 00:39:14,000
This mint one is a bit strong.

495
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:16,167
So? You don't like it?

496
00:39:16,167 --> 00:39:18,900
No, that's why I like it even more.

497
00:39:25,900 --> 00:39:30,667
Darn it, I'm telling you to listen
while I'm still being nice!

498
00:39:30,667 --> 00:39:31,967
Is it hard to understand?

499
00:39:31,967 --> 00:39:34,233
- I'll lose the case.
- Look at you.

500
00:39:34,233 --> 00:39:36,667
I'll lose the case. I'll lose...

501
00:39:36,667 --> 00:39:39,300
- My phone... I need my phone.
- Your phone?

502
00:39:39,300 --> 00:39:40,600
- I need my phone.
- Fine.

503
00:39:40,600 --> 00:39:44,867
Lose the case, and I'll give your phone back.

504
00:39:51,767 --> 00:39:55,433
You piece of work! You punk! Darn it!

505
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:06,333
Hey, you punk!

506
00:40:11,300 --> 00:40:12,967
You punk!

507
00:40:20,233 --> 00:40:21,933
You piece of work!

508
00:40:23,200 --> 00:40:25,367
Give it back! You punk!

509
00:40:34,033 --> 00:40:36,433
You piece of work! You're dead.

510
00:40:39,667 --> 00:40:42,633
You punk!

511
00:40:50,933 --> 00:40:53,200
Stop, you punk!

512
00:40:59,767 --> 00:41:03,200
I'll kill you if I catch you.

513
00:41:14,100 --> 00:41:17,567
I'll tear you apart
when I get my hands on you. You punk!

514
00:41:21,033 --> 00:41:22,900
[Min Seo's Academy]

515
00:41:25,700 --> 00:41:28,033
Darn it, jeez...

516
00:41:28,033 --> 00:41:29,408
[Min Seo's Academy]

517
00:42:18,367 --> 00:42:23,533
[Accident Occurred, March 30, 9:04 PM]

518
00:42:23,533 --> 00:42:26,100
Yeah, yeah. You can stop here.

519
00:42:28,533 --> 00:42:30,333
Thank you!

520
00:42:38,800 --> 00:42:41,700
What? Why is this open?

521
00:42:43,600 --> 00:42:47,267
Huh? What? Where did it go?

522
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:50,467
Huh? What happened to this?

523
00:42:52,233 --> 00:42:55,233
Who did this? Seriously...

524
00:42:56,700 --> 00:42:59,633
What kind of punk did this?

525
00:42:59,633 --> 00:43:01,767
Jeez, seriously...

526
00:43:03,733 --> 00:43:05,133
What happened?

527
00:43:05,133 --> 00:43:07,933
Oh, Ye Ji, what happened to my car?

528
00:43:07,933 --> 00:43:09,433
Did you hear anything?

529
00:43:09,433 --> 00:43:11,100
Dad...

530
00:43:23,800 --> 00:43:25,567
Min Seo?

531
00:43:26,833 --> 00:43:29,667
What are you doing there? Why...

532
00:43:30,533 --> 00:43:36,200
Mom... if we go back now,
that man might still survive.

533
00:43:36,200 --> 00:43:38,000
We have to hurry.

534
00:43:39,367 --> 00:43:41,633
What are you talking about?

535
00:43:41,633 --> 00:43:45,300
Explain it so I can understand.

536
00:43:45,933 --> 00:43:48,500
What do I do?

537
00:43:51,933 --> 00:43:55,333
Ye Ji, what's wrong?

538
00:43:55,333 --> 00:43:57,100
Did something happen?

539
00:44:00,233 --> 00:44:02,067
I...

540
00:44:02,067 --> 00:44:05,867
I mean, I...

541
00:44:05,867 --> 00:44:09,267
I...

542
00:44:09,267 --> 00:44:11,700
I drove your car...

543
00:44:12,900 --> 00:44:15,200
I hit that man with a car...

544
00:44:16,167 --> 00:44:18,233
Because of me...
